# BUG-593: the Resolver's statement walker skipped a numeric `for`, `allocate`, `in`,
# `require` / `ensure` and the `for ... if` filter, so an undefined name inside any of them
# passed `zebra -c` and failed inside zig. One per kind that a plain program can hold.
def main()
    for i in 0 .. 3
        print(nope_fornum)
    allocate Arena()
        print(nope_allocate)
    for x in [1, 2] if x > nope_filter
        print(x)
